data/board.port
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ops/ (VPS alerting layer, imported 2026-08-31 from /root/ops/scripts/ on
# the VPS) — CODE only is tracked. Runtime data — state files, logs, and
# pre-edit backup snapshots — is never committed, matching the convention
# already in place on the VPS itself (.bak-* files, /root/ops/state/).
ops/state/
ops/**/*.bak
ops/**/*.bak-*
ops/**/*.bak.*
ops/**/*.log
ops/backups/

# Paid third-party course corpora. Every EXTRACTION_LOG in here states
# "sources/ is gitignored — local-only, never committed, never public,
# never free." That was true as policy and false as configuration: the
# directory was merely untracked, so a single `git add -A` at repo root
# would have staged 342 files of watermarked, licensed course material.
# Verified 2026-08-19. The rule is now enforced, not just documented.
METHODS/seo-geo/sources/
